WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:06.399
So my goal, my priority since the start of
the coronavirus pandemic has been to be accurately

00:00:06.399 --> 00:00:11.049
alarmist for the information that we have,
and there was a period back in, I think it

00:00:11.049 --> 00:00:15.930
was December, January, where I was getting
emails from people saying, David, you're overly

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:18.540
alarmist, this isn't going to be anything.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:23.300
And then there was maybe a little period,
sort of like in May, where I was maybe more

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.180
optimistic about the situation than some in
the audience.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:34.050
But I think that I've done an OK job at more
or less accurately communicating the sort

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:38.160
of status of the situation and the outlook
with the pandemic.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:45.130
And I have what I think is some accurately
but cautiously optimistic news for you today.

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:50.120
And although the timing of it is interesting,
this is not a political comment, but there

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:58.399
is a mathematical coincidence pointing to
a case and death peak, hopefully the last

00:00:58.399 --> 00:01:01.680
one of the pandemic right around the time
of Joe Biden's inauguration.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.290
Now, I'm not making a political segment out
of this.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:09.650
It's mere coincidence when we I'll show you
the math and the trajectories.

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:14.140
But it seems as though right around January
20th, the day that Joe Biden will be sworn

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:21.980
in as president, that we will be starting
to get past what is hopefully the last peak

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:23.120
of this pandemic.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:25.410
And again, it's a coincidence.

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:31.350
I'm not claiming January 20th, Joe Biden will
be sworn in and covid will be fixed.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:33.660
It is merely a timing coincidence.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:38.810
And we know that these peaks depend on what
happens in the weeks and months leading up.

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:43.210
But I want to go through it with you because
it does feel like we're starting to get into

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:44.210
the tunnel.

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:46.300
At least we're maybe seeing the light or maybe
not.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:50.660
But we're definitely in the part of the tunnel
that we would consider the latter part of

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:51.660
the tunnel.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:56.370
Now, as you may know, we've had three coronavirus
peaks in the United States.

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:57.730
Many countries have only had two.

00:01:57.730 --> 00:01:59.300
We've had three.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:00.600
First one was in April.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:01.870
Second one was in July.

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:03.960
And the third one is right now.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:08.810
And in this third peak, we've seen cases spike
all the way up to close to two hundred and

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:13.909
fifty thousand cases in a single day, mostly
in the low to 100th to ten, two hundred and

00:02:13.909 --> 00:02:14.909
fifteen thousand.

00:02:14.909 --> 00:02:18.519
And what you can also see when looking at
the case graph, if you're watching along with

00:02:18.519 --> 00:02:24.569
me today is that over the last 10 days, the
rate of case growth has slowed down, meaning

00:02:24.569 --> 00:02:29.030
the curve flattened and it even turned downwards
in the last few days.

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:35.189
Now, it is quite possible that there's still
one more peak to go, fueled by holiday and

00:02:35.189 --> 00:02:37.939
end of year travel and indoor gatherings.

00:02:37.939 --> 00:02:39.739
We shouldn't do them.

00:02:39.739 --> 00:02:43.040
It's sort of a foregone conclusion that no
matter what I say, many people are going to

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:44.040
do them.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:50.390
But the rate of case growth in the US at at
a large, broad level is slowing down.

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:54.480
Looking at the predictions in the models from
a variety of epidemiologists and other experts,

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:59.921
that case peak is expected to be right around
the end of the of the first week of January,

00:02:59.921 --> 00:03:03.209
January seven, eight, nine, 10, 11, 12.

00:03:03.209 --> 00:03:04.680
Very rough estimate.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:08.980
And we know that deaths lag cases by about
three weeks.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:14.420
And when you look at the death chart right
now, you see a similar pattern to cases.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:22.469
And while in this third peak, we've started
to see the cases come down a bit, we are only

00:03:22.469 --> 00:03:25.620
seeing the growth of deaths slow down.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:31.359
So we likely are about three weeks behind
in terms of deaths where we are in cases.

00:03:31.359 --> 00:03:37.409
So if we see a case peak around it January
10th to pick a date, we would expect to see

00:03:37.409 --> 00:03:40.870
a death peak right around February one in
all likelihood.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:43.489
And this doesn't justify getting careless.

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:49.249
It doesn't do anything to change the tragic
death and destruction that the virus has already

00:03:49.249 --> 00:03:50.249
brought to date.

00:03:50.249 --> 00:03:56.620
But in all likelihood, that in January will
be the final peak of this pandemic unless

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:58.529
something dramatic changes.

00:03:58.529 --> 00:03:59.609
Why?

00:03:59.609 --> 00:04:04.340
Because that will not only be the worst moment
in terms of weather and people being indoors.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:09.499
December, January is the coldest time of the
year in the parts of the U.S. that have winter.

00:04:09.499 --> 00:04:13.749
But as the temperature warms and the days
get longer and people spend more time outside,

00:04:13.749 --> 00:04:16.829
we will also have the benefit of the vaccination
program.

00:04:16.829 --> 00:04:18.489
Vaccination has started in the U.S.

00:04:18.489 --> 00:04:22.510
We have the approved vaccine from Pfizer,
emergency use approval.

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:26.980
Second vaccine from Moderna expected to be
approved for emergency use tomorrow.

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:29.550
Third vaccine maybe in the first quarter of
the new year.

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:33.340
So at the same time that we will be peaking
in cases and deaths with the coldest weather

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:38.460
in the most people indoors, we will have,
if all goes to plan, all health care workers

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:43.780
vaccinated by February 1st, all nursing home
residents vaccinated by February 1st.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:48.590
And we will be in the process of vaccinating
that next most vulnerable group, which will

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:53.720
include the oldest folks and those with the
most serious comorbidities, and by protecting

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:58.800
an additional five to seven percent of the
population each month, starting now.

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:05.490
Going into January, February, March, that
peak we're expecting in January is likely

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:10.409
to be the final one and have a more rapid
decline than without vaccination.

00:05:10.409 --> 00:05:14.669
So this is all excellent news, but there is
still a big battle here.

00:05:14.669 --> 00:05:18.140
We're still going to have to do all the things
we've been many of us have been doing.

00:05:18.140 --> 00:05:25.110
Not all of us masks, social distancing, avoiding
indoor gatherings, but it is mathematically

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:31.090
looking like we're potentially about three
weeks from the case, peak of the pandemic

00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:33.250
and five to six weeks from the death peak.

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:39.080
And at that point, the vaccination program
will be more robust with millions of vaccinations

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:40.080
weekly.

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:41.530
So there is a light there.

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:42.530
That's the good news.

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:48.750
Now, given this, we should be extra cautious
in these next months because we're so close.

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:53.650
It's not like, listen, this is going to go
on for two or three more years and we might

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:58.750
be well, for psychological reasons, maybe
we take a screw it attitude and just have

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:00.319
a good time.

00:06:00.319 --> 00:06:05.259
Starting now, we will see five ish percent
of the country vaccinated each month.

00:06:05.259 --> 00:06:06.360
That's huge.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:10.550
And we are close to deaths and cases starting
to decline.

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:13.139
So the messages, that's the math of it.

00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:18.039
Those are the expectations that were vaccination
is we're just a couple months away from significantly

00:06:18.039 --> 00:06:19.930
better circumstances, my friends.

00:06:19.930 --> 00:07:35.580
So let's do everything that we can.

